tritional Support Community: Artificial Nutrition and Related Therapies\n\nThe community focuses on various forms of artificial nutrition, including enteral and parenteral methods, and their applications in managing patients with specific medical conditions. Key entities include nutritional interventions, medications, and medical professionals involved in the care of patients requiring nutritional support.\n\n## Artificial Nutrition as a Critical Intervention\n\nArtificial nutrition is essential for patients unable to consume food orally, particularly in critical care settings. It encompasses both enteral and parenteral nutrition methods, which are vital for preventing malnutrition and supporting recovery in patients with severe health issues. The need for artificial nutrition arises in various conditions, including cancer, liver diseases, and acute pancreatitis, highlighting its importance in clinical practice. [Data: Entities (1635, 4586, 2602, 6756, 6759); Relationships (3116, 4586, 2602, 6756, 6759)]\n\n## Role of Medications in Nutritional Support\n\nMedications such as Fluconazole and Itraconazole are often prescribed to patients receiving nutritional support to manage infections that can complicate their nutritional status. These antifungal medications are particularly important for immunocompromised patients, such as those undergoing cancer treatment, where maintaining nutritional intake is crucial for recovery. The integration of pharmacological interventions with nutritional support is essential for comprehensive patient care. [Data: Entities (2285, 2286); Relationships (3104, 3105)]\n\n## Hyponatremia and Nutritional Support\n\nHyponatremia is a common complication in patients receiving artificial nutrition, often necessitating careful monitoring and management of sodium levels. This condition can arise due to fluid overload and electrolyte imbalances during nutritional support. Effective management strategies are critical to prevent complications associated with hyponatremia, particularly in patients with complex health conditions. [Data: Entities (1635); Relationships (6817, 6812)]\n\n## Pediatric Considerations in Artificial Nutrition\n\nNutritional support in pediatric patients requires specialized approaches, including enteral and parenteral nutrition tailored to their unique needs. Guidelines and protocols for pediatric nutrition are essential to ensure that children receive adequate dietary support, particularly in cases of severe health issues or after surgical interventions. The focus on pediatric nutritional needs highlights the importance of tailored care in this demographic. [Data: Entities (1651, 1652); Relationships (6766, 6827)]\n\n## Impact of Nutritional Support on Cancer Patients\n\nCancer patients often face significant challenges in maintaining nutritional intake due to the effects of their condition and treatment. Artificial nutrition plays a crucial role in managing these patients, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery. The relationship between cancer treatment and nutritional support underscores the importance of integrated care strategies in oncology. [Data: Entities (1635); Relationships (6760, 6806)]\n\n## Nutritional Support for Patients with Inflammatory Conditions\n\nPatients with inflammatory bowel diseases and other inflammatory conditions may require specialized nutritional management to address their dietary needs. Artificial nutrition can be a critical component of their treatment plan, helping to prevent malnutrition and support recovery. The focus on inflammatory conditions highlights the diverse applications of nutritional support in clinical practice. [Data: Entities (1635); Relationships (6756, 6800)]\n\n## The Role of Healthcare Professionals in Nutritional Support\n\nHealthcare professionals, including dietitians and medical doctors, play a vital role in planning and managing artificial nutrition for patients. Their expertise is essential in assessing nutritional needs, developing treatment plans, and monitoring patient progress. The collaborative approach among healthcare providers is crucial for ensuring effective nutritional support and improving patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (2198, 1635); Relationships (6803, 6806)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2370,NE,\"NE, or Nutrición Enteral, refers to a method of providing nutrition directly through the gastrointestinal tract via a tube. This approach is particularly beneficial for patients who cannot eat by mouth due to various medical conditions, including neurological impairments that affect swallowing. NE encompasses several specific applications, such as nocturnal enteral nutrition, which delivers nutrition during the night, and nutritional enteral feeding, which is often used in severe cases like pancreatitis.\n\nThe method is designed to meet the caloric requirements of patients and is commonly utilized in critical care settings. It is less associated with complications such as hyponatremia compared to parenteral nutrition, making it a preferred option when the digestive tract is functional. Nutritional formulas used in NE are especially important in oncology settings and for patients with swallowing difficulties.\n\nOverall, NE serves as a crucial nutritional support system, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients directly into their stomach or intestines when oral intake is not possible.\",24\r\n2371,NP,\"NP refers to Nutritional Parenteral, a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who cannot tolerate enteral feeding, effectively bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This approach is particularly relevant for patient groups, including those who have undergone abdominal surgery related to digestive neoplasia, and may experience complications such as nausea and pain. In clinical settings, NP has been studied in relation to various factors, including its correlation with hospital stay duration in patients with hyponatremia. Nutritional practices and guidelines for NP emphasize the use of different lipid sources and amino acids to optimize patient care, especially in critical care environments. Overall, NP serves as a vital nutritional support system for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through traditional means.\",14\r\n6393,SNO,\"SNO refers to oral nutritional supplements designed to support the dietary needs of patients, particularly those at risk of malnutrition. These specialized nutritional supplements are administered orally and are particularly beneficial for patients with malnutrition, those preparing for surgery, and individuals managing diabetes. SNO encompasses a range of nutritional formulas tailored to enhance dietary intake, providing essential calories and nutrients necessary for recovery and overall health. Additionally, SNO includes specific nutritional support for patients undergoing cancer treatment, ensuring that their unique dietary requirements are met. Overall, SNO plays a crucial role in improving the nutritional status of patients in various medical contexts.\",10\r\n7073,GRP,\"GRP refers to a prophylactic gastrostomy placement that was requested for the patient, serving as a medical intervention to provide nutritional support. This type of feeding tube is utilized for patients who are unable to take food orally, indicating its importance in ensuring adequate nutrition. The gastrostomy route through which the patient received this nutritional support is critical for their recovery post-surgery, highlighting the essential role of GRP in the patient's overall treatment plan.\",4\r\n2304,CICATRIZACIÓN,\"CICATRIZACIÓN refers to the process of wound healing, which is particularly crucial for patients who have suffered burns. This healing process necessitates adequate protein intake to support recovery. Additionally, wound healing is essential for patients undergoing surgical procedures, especially those related to head and neck tumors. The effectiveness of cicatrización is significantly influenced by nutritional support, highlighting the importance of proper dietary management in promoting recovery for these patients.\",3\r\n7081,RT,\"RT refers to radiotherapy, a treatment that can lead to complications such as mucositis in patients. Additionally, it is noted that the patient underwent RT, which affected their appetite and weight.\",2\r\n2486,FÓRMULAS HIPERCALÓRICAS,\"FÓRMULAS HIPERCALÓRICAS son preparaciones nutricionales específicamente diseñadas para ofrecer un alto contenido calórico. Estas fórmulas son especialmente útiles para pacientes que presentan descompensación hidrópica y son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay un aumento de las necesidades calóricas, como en el caso de pacientes con desnutrición. Su objetivo principal es proporcionar la energía necesaria para apoyar la recuperación y el bienestar de estos pacientes.\",4\r\n4371,FLUIDOTERAPIA,\"FLUIDOTERAPIA, or fluid therapy, is a vital medical treatment that involves the administration of fluids to patients to maintain hydration and electrolyte balance. It is particularly crucial for burn patients, where it focuses on hydration to ensure vital organ perfusion and manage shock. Additionally, fluid therapy plays an important role in managing diabetic ketoacidosis (cetoacidosis diabética). The practice is also commonly utilized in surgical contexts to support patients' hydration needs and overall stability during and after procedures.\",3\r\n4969,EDUCACIÓN NUTRICIONAL,\"\"\"Educación nutricional\"\" refers to the process of educating patients about proper dietary practices to manage their health conditions, particularly diabetes. It encompasses teaching individuals about healthy eating habits and the significance of nutrition in maintaining overall health and preventing diseases. Additionally, nutritional education plays a crucial role in the treatment of patients with eating disorders, as it helps them understand and adopt healthy eating patterns. Overall, educación nutricional is essential for promoting better health outcomes through informed dietary choices.\",3\r\n13180,PACIENTE QUEMADO,\"The \"\"PACIENTE QUEMADO\"\" refers to a burn patient who is suffering from severe burns and requires specific nutritional assessment and support. Due to the effects of burns on metabolism and nutrition, this patient necessitates specialized nutritional support and fluid therapy to aid in their recovery.\",18\r\n1636,PACIENTE QUIRÚRGICO,\"The \"\"PACIENTE QUIRÚRGICO\"\" refers to an individual who is undergoing a surgical procedure. This type of patient may benefit from specific nutritional formulas designed to enhance their recovery process. Specialized nutritional support is often necessary for these patients to ensure optimal healing and overall health following surgery.\",3\r\n1811,GLUCOSADO 30%,\"GLUCOSADO 30% is an intravenous solution containing 30% glucose, specifically designed to meet the intensive energy needs of patients.\",2\r\n1812,GLUCOSADO 40%,\"Glucosado 40% is a specialized intravenous glucose solution that contains a concentration of 40% glucose. It is primarily utilized in nutritional support, particularly for patients with critical energy requirements. This solution serves as an essential resource in medical settings, providing necessary energy to individuals who may be unable to meet their nutritional needs through regular dietary intake.\",2\r\n2297,ONDANSETRÓN,\"Ondansetron, also known as Ondansetrón, is an antiemetic medication that serves to prevent nausea and vomiting, particularly those induced by cancer treatments. It functions as a 5HT3 antagonist, effectively reducing the incidence of nausea and vomiting associated with such therapies.\",2\r\n7010,DRFQ,\"DRFQ refers to a specific type of diabetes diagnosed in patients, necessitating management and treatment strategies that include insulin administration and nutritional educati